---
// P10 — YouthWIDE /programs/youthwide/ (T3 conversion page; doc 04 matrices 4.1, 4.2 and 4.3; C1 → C14).
// One page for both audiences (WP4c: NationWIDE was renamed YouthWIDE and merged in). WP30d (owner direction 2026-10-14: less is more, global first): the page leads with the
// co-funded country cohorts (funders and development partners; the program is designed for South Asia, the Middle East and North Africa, and Sub-Saharan Africa) and gives the Bangladesh initiative
// ONE band of its own (#governments, linked from the Governments partner page and a case study). Cut as report-like: In Short, the definition band, the priority-group cards, the
// delivery grid, the work-entry plans, the roadmap and reporting timelines, the RACI and decision sheet, the comparison table, the offer notes and the four gain rows of the C8 map.
// Kept because a gate or a registered claim needs them: the three ranked pains (C2) and one C8 row each, the positioning statement opening C6, both session agendas, the trial relevance
// qualifiers and every scope word.
// WP36 (cycle-13 reviews): "Our Approach" states what the program does (training, mentoring and placement support in existing labs and colleges, monthly reports) and no longer restates the audience and the regions the hero
// and the glance already give; scripts/check-facts.mjs declares that statement for this page (POSITION_WHOLE_STATEMENT). The Bangladesh band says "Designed for delivery through existing government digital labs
// and colleges", and the glance's Delivery row says "a central team coordinating local labs for larger programs" in place of "hub-and-spoke" (as Our Model does).
// WP39 (cycle-16 review): the hero lead is one sentence (audience, outcome and mechanism; the scope word "as agreed in the program scope" moved to the glance's Reporting row); the three-card C8 band (IncludesBand) replaces the
// funder concern / what is included / practical benefit matrix; "Choose Your Entry Point" keeps both route actions and the procurement sentence and has ONE agenda line under the two cards in place of two near-identical agendas.
// WP40 (cycle-17 review): the glance row that says where the program is designed to run is headed "Designed for Three Regions" ("Where It Runs" read as a list of countries where it runs today); the timing question uses the
// two-sentence variant (Q7-model), because "What Happens Next" below shows the sequence the shared answer counted out week by week.
// WP41 (cycle-18 review): the "What Success Looks Like" band (#future) is about young people earning ("Young People Earning, Locally and Globally": jobs, freelance clients and businesses of their own); the monthly
// reports it used to describe are already in the glance's Reporting row and the C8 cards, so it no longer explains them a third time.
// WP48 (cycle-23 reviews, consistent with the owner decision of 2026-10-15 for the audience pages): the page no longer repeats Home's persuasion bands. The Cost of Waiting band ("Training Without Work Entry Leaves Budgets Without Results", #cost)
// and the Imagine band ("Young People Earning, Locally and Globally", #future) are gone, and so are the hero's two links back to audience pages ("For Development Partners", "For Governments"; the ministry briefing stays beside the one button).
// The challenge band stays, then the track record and the delivery model; the tone alternates white, airy, white, airy, Klein. The Bangladesh band's labs tile (GV-09) shows the register's qualifier as its note (lab access and seats are confirmed per program).
// WP49 (cycle-24 review): the closing paragraph under "What Happens Next" (PD-04 in full: "For grant-funded pilots: Discovery (Week 1) → Co-Design (Week 2) → Agreement (Week 3), ...; training starts 6–8 weeks after signing. Public procurement follows the agency’s own timeline.") is gone: it repeated
// the step sequence above it and the timing question in the FAQ (Q7-model). The procurement sentence is still on the page, in the Governments entry card and in that answer; the risk band's eyebrow is "Managed Rollout".
// WP50 (cycle-25 review): step 4 of "What Happens Next" says "Training starts in existing labs and colleges on the agreed schedule." (it pointed at "the window below", which WP49 had removed).
// WP51 (cycle-26 review): the options lead no longer describes the website ("Program options are shown without prices; the indicative budget is shared in the discovery session."): it says "We share an indicative budget in the discovery session."
// WP52 (cycle-27 reviews, Claude): the hero's ministry-briefing text link is labelled with its audience, "Governments: Request a Briefing for Your Ministry" (the label sits outside the link, as in CTABand's `routes`; the one primary button is unchanged);
// the glance's first row says "Bangladesh is where most delivery has been" where it said "Bangladesh is the reference implementation" (IN-02 says it the same way; the Bangladesh band's heading, "Reference Country and 2030 Aim", is unchanged).
import ProgramGlance from '../../components/pages/programs/ProgramGlance.astro';
import LandingLayout from '../../layouts/LandingLayout.astro';
import Section from '../../components/ui/Section.astro';
import SectionHeader from '../../components/ui/SectionHeader.astro';
import SessionAgenda from '../../components/ui/SessionAgenda.astro';
import EmailFallback from '../../components/ui/EmailFallback.astro';
import PhotoGallery from '../../components/ui/PhotoGallery.astro';
import Hero from '../../components/system/Hero.astro';
import Button from '../../components/system/Button.astro';
import StatusTag from '../../components/system/StatusTag.astro';
import Icon from '../../components/system/Icon.astro';
import FactStat from '../../components/facts/FactStat.astro';
import EvidenceBand from '../../components/pages/home/EvidenceBand.astro';
import CaseStudyCarousel from '../../components/sections/CaseStudyCarousel.astro';
import IncludesBand from '../../components/sections/IncludesBand.astro';
import GainsPains from '../../components/pages/partners/GainsPains.astro';
import CopyP from '../../components/pages/programs/CopyP.astro';
import ProblemSection from '../../components/pages/programs/ProblemSection.astro';
import GuideSection from '../../components/pages/programs/GuideSection.astro';
import MechanismSection from '../../components/pages/programs/MechanismSection.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/pages/programs/FaqSection.astro';
import OfferSection from '../../components/pages/programs/OfferSection.astro';
import RiskSection from '../../components/pages/programs/RiskSection.astro';
import NextSteps from '../../components/pages/programs/NextSteps.astro';
import { faqNode, type FaqSource } from '../../components/pages/programs/faq';
import { C14_FIRST, ctaFor, serviceNode, statValue } from '../../components/pages/programs/meta';
import { C14, FUNDER_PAINS, MICRO_COMMITMENT, POSITIONING, PROGRAM_OPTIONS, SAFEGUARDING, painForList, painForRow } from '../../data/copy';
import { fact } from '../../data/facts';
import { galleryPhotos } from '../../data/photos';
import { formatDate, isoDate } from '../../lib/format';
import { webPage } from '../../lib/schema';
import { url } from '../../lib/url';

const path = '/programs/youthwide/';
const LAST_UPDATED = '2026-10-15'; // WP31: the cycle-8 review wording changes
const title = 'YouthWIDE: From Training to Paid Digital Work';
const description = 'YouthWIDE prepares educated, unemployed youth for paid digital work: co-funded cohorts designed for three regions, with a 2030 aim in Bangladesh.';
const discovery = ctaFor('discovery');
const briefing = ctaFor('briefing');
const cofunding = ctaFor('nationalFunding');
const nationalSize = PROGRAM_OPTIONS[2].size.split(' ')[0];
const hours = statValue('PD-01');

// Five decision questions, one to three sentences each (cost is answered in the options band). Longer answers live on the evidence pages and in the discovery session.
const faqSources: FaqSource[] = [
  { q: 'Is YouthWIDE Right for Our Organization?', html: `Right for you if you want employment outcomes tracked after blended training delivered through existing labs and colleges. YouthWIDE is not the right fit if you need a ${nationalSize} rollout delivered by one provider in a single phase; we plan national delivery phase by phase.`, evidence: ['PD-05'] },
  { q: 'Will This Work in Our Country?', html: 'That depends on local demand, which we test first. Our outcome evidence comes mainly from Bangladesh, and the Kosovo pilot adds program results from outside it. CodersTrust has run programs since 2014 in 15 countries and territories.', evidence: ['SC-03', 'IN-02', 'PD-10', 'PR-02'] },
  {
    q: 'Can You Deliver at National Scale?',
    html: `Her Power, a national program of DoICT, the ICT Division, trained 25,125 women across 130 sub-districts (upazilas). CodersTrust provided the curriculum, training manuals and mentorship guidelines and trained 2,500 women directly.</p><p data-fact="PD-06 PD-05">We scale in phases, up to 10 cohorts in parallel, with certified local facilitators. A ${nationalSize} phase is a design option; we have not yet delivered a program at that size.`,
    evidence: ['GV-01', 'GV-11'],
  },
  { q: 'How Do You Prove Outcomes?', html: 'As agreed in the program scope, we plan a baseline at enrollment, follow-up surveys at 3, 6 and 12 months and monthly reports for every cohort, with documentary evidence of earnings where available. Independent evaluation is welcome.', evidence: ['PD-09', 'PD-08', 'RC-01'] },
  { audience: 'variants' as const, id: 'Q7-model' },
];

const jsonLd = [
  webPage({ path, name: 'YouthWIDE — From Training to Paid Digital Work', description, dateModified: LAST_UPDATED, breadcrumb: [{ name: 'Home', path: '/' }, { name: 'Programs', path: '/programs/' }, { name: 'YouthWIDE', path }] }),
  serviceNode({ path, name: 'YouthWIDE', description: fact('IN-02').text, audience: 'Ministries, agencies, development partners and funders', areaServed: ['Bangladesh', 'South Asia', 'Middle East and North Africa', 'Sub-Saharan Africa'] }),
  faqNode(faqSources, path),
];

const measures = ['Completion', 'Certification', 'First paid work', 'Sustained work', 'Cost per completer and per verified outcome'];
---

<LandingLayout title={title} description={description} path={path} breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Programs', href: '/programs/' }, { label: 'YouthWIDE' }]} jsonLd={jsonLd} stickyCta={discovery}>
  <!-- C1 -->
  <!-- WP20c: the ministry briefing is a text link beside the one primary button (not a second button) -->
  <div id="hero">
    <Hero
      eyebrow="YouthWIDE · Youth Digital Employment Program"
      title="From Training to Paid Digital Work, Country by Country"
      lead="YouthWIDE helps governments and funders prepare educated, unemployed youth for paid digital work through training, mentoring and placement support."
      artSeed="youthwide"
    >
      <Fragment slot="actions">
        <Button href={discovery.href} iconEnd="arrow-right">{discovery.label}</Button>
        {
          briefing.href && (
            <nav class="routes" aria-label="Other Ways to Start">
              <span class="route">Governments: <a class="link" href={briefing.href}>{briefing.label}<Icon name="arrow-right" size={16} /></a></span>
            </nav>
          )
        }
      </Fragment>
    </Hero>
  </div>

  <ProgramGlance
    title="YouthWIDE at a Glance"
    rows={[
      // WP45 (cycle-21 review): IN-01 is an initiative that AIMS to train 2 million vulnerable youth by 2030, not an existing national program, so the row says "aims" (and the figure is the band's tile below, not retyped here).
      // WP48 (cycle-23 review): the row says "2 million vulnerable youth", IN-01's own wording, as the Programs menu, Home and the Programs hub do.
      { label: 'Designed for Three Regions', text: 'South Asia, the Middle East and North Africa, and Sub-Saharan Africa, as co-funded country cohorts. Bangladesh is where most delivery has been, with an initiative of its own that aims to train 2 million vulnerable youth by 2030.', facts: ['IN-02', 'IN-01'] },
      { label: 'Who It Is For', text: 'Governments, development partners and funders who want to report on educated, unemployed young people moving into paid digital work.' },
      { label: 'Delivery', text: 'Blended training in existing labs and colleges, with certified local facilitators; a central team coordinating local labs for larger programs.', facts: ['PD-06'] },
      { label: 'Training and Mentoring', text: `${hours} training hours per certification with the exam fee included, then three months of milestone-based mentoring.`, facts: ['PD-01', 'PD-02', 'PD-02a'] },
      { label: 'Placement Support', text: 'Placement support into local, remote and global work.', facts: ['PD-15'] },
      { label: 'Reporting', text: 'Monthly reports, follow-up surveys and documentary evidence of earnings where available, as agreed in the program scope.', facts: ['PD-08', 'PD-09'] },
    ]}
  />

  <!-- C2 (ranked pains P1–P3, checked by scripts/check-facts.mjs) -->
  <ProblemSection eyebrow="The Challenge" title="Education Alone Is Not Getting Young People into Work" factIds={['PX-01', 'PX-02']}>
    <GainsPains painsHeading="What Gets in the Way" pains={FUNDER_PAINS.map(painForList)} />
  </ProblemSection>

  <!-- C3 (Cost of Waiting) is left to Home since WP48 (cycle-23 review, consistent with the owner decision of 2026-10-15). -->

  <!-- C5 (credibility before the vision) -->
  <GuideSection
    title={`We Have Built This Path Since ${statValue('ID-02')}`}
    statIds={['SC-01', 'SC-03']}
    partnerGroup={['government', 'academic', 'development']}
    method={{ text: 'TalentLEAP organizes skills into career paths.', factId: 'IN-06', link: { label: 'How TalentLEAP Works', href: '/our-model/talentleap/' } }}
  />

  <!-- C4 (Imagine) is left to Home since WP48 (cycle-23 review, consistent with the owner decision of 2026-10-15). -->

  <!-- C6 (the positioning statement opens the band) -->
  <MechanismSection
    title="One Delivery Model, from Selection to Paid Work"
    positioning={POSITIONING.youthwide}
    blocks={[
      { label: 'Who We Reach', title: 'Educated, Unemployed and Underemployed Youth', text: 'Priority groups are agreed with you in co-design; women are a priority in every group.', icon: 'users' },
      { label: 'How We Reach Them', title: 'Accessible Selection, Blended Delivery', text: 'Outreach and an accessible readiness assessment, then training in existing labs and colleges.', icon: 'graduation-cap' },
      { label: 'What We Deliver', title: 'AI-Ready Training, Certification Preparation and Mentoring', text: 'Each track prepares learners for an industry certification, then three months of milestone-based mentoring; exam eligibility and attempts are agreed in the program scope.', icon: 'award' },
      { label: 'Where They Work', title: 'Local, Remote, Overseas and Freelance Work', text: 'Placement support and outcome tracking after each course.', icon: 'globe' },
    ]}
    factIds={['PD-14', 'PD-06', 'PD-01', 'PD-02', 'PD-15']}
    link={{ label: 'How Our Model Works', href: '/our-model/' }}
  />

  <!-- The Bangladesh initiative: one band (WP30d), built from the shared C6 band (eyebrow, headline, one paragraph, proof, text link). #governments is linked from the Governments partner page and a case study.
       WP45 (cycle-21 review): headed "Reference Country and 2030 Aim", not "The National Initiative", which read as an existing national program (IN-01 is an initiative that aims to train 2 million vulnerable youth by 2030). -->
  <MechanismSection
    id="governments"
    tone="airy"
    eyebrow="For Governments and Ministries"
    title="Bangladesh: Reference Country and 2030 Aim"
    lead="Designed for delivery through existing government digital labs and colleges; lab access and seats are confirmed per program."
    link={{ label: cofunding.label, href: cofunding.href }}
  >
    <div class="mech-stats">
      <div class="mech-target" data-reveal>
        <StatusTag status="Target" />
        <FactStat id="IN-01" />
        <p class="mech-target__note">A national ambition for 2030 that depends on government and donor commitments; not a delivered figure.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="mech-stat"><FactStat id="GV-09" /></div>
      <div class="mech-stat"><StatusTag status="Delivered" /><FactStat id="GV-13" /></div>
    </div>
  </MechanismSection>

  <!-- C7 -->
  <EvidenceBand
    id="proof-band"
    title="Trial and Survey Evidence"
    bandHeading="Trial and Survey Evidence"
    trialHeading="An Independent Randomized Trial"
    headlineFact="RC-01"
    chart="trial"
    chip={false}
    trialSentence
    lead="Trial figures are for a predecessor program. Survey figures are among surveyed completers, from the October 2026 survey."
    statIds={['RC-02']}
    surveyStatIds={['OC-03']}
    links={[{ label: 'Impact Survey 2026', href: '/impact/outcomes-2026/' }, { label: 'The Randomized Trial', href: '/impact/independent-evaluation/' }]}
  />
  <CaseStudyCarousel
    id="cases"
    eyebrow="Proof in Practice"
    title="Results from Delivered Programs"
    items={[
      { title: 'Women’s Skill Development for Freelancing Marketplace (WSDFM)', program: 'Commissioned by Porticus', factId: 'PR-01', href: '/impact/case-studies/wsdfm-women-freelancers/' },
      { title: 'Women in Online Work, Kosovo', program: 'World Bank Group', factId: 'PR-02', href: '/impact/case-studies/kosovo-women-in-online-work/' },
      { title: 'Her Power', program: 'ICT Division / Department of ICT (DoICT)', factId: 'PR-05', href: '/impact/case-studies/her-power/' },
    ]}
  />

  <!-- C8: one card per ranked pain of C2 (pain → how we relieve it → the registered facts behind it), checked by scripts/check-facts.mjs (`data-relieves`).
       WP39 (cycle-16 review): three short cards in place of the funder concern / what is included / practical benefit matrix; the sentences keep the matrix rows' words (PD-15, PD-01 and PD-19: placement support, three months
       of milestone-based mentoring, a work-entry plan per track approved before enrollment; PD-08 and PD-09: the baseline, monthly reports, follow-up surveys, documentary evidence where available; PD-02 and PD-10: an
       AI-ready curriculum, entry-level tracks set per country from employer demand). -->
  <IncludesBand
    title="Built Around What Funders and Agencies Ask"
    cards={[
      {
        painId: painForRow(FUNDER_PAINS, 'P1').painId,
        icon: 'route',
        title: 'Placement Support and Mentoring',
        text: 'Placement support, three months of milestone-based mentoring and a work-entry plan per track approved before enrollment. Success is measured against agreed outcomes, including paid work, not attendance alone.',
        facts: ['PD-15', 'PD-01', 'PD-19'],
      },
      {
        painId: painForRow(FUNDER_PAINS, 'P2').painId,
        icon: 'clipboard-check',
        title: 'Results Your Evaluators Can Check',
        text: 'A baseline, monthly reports and follow-up surveys, as agreed in the program scope. Your evaluators can check results against payslips, offer letters, platform logs or bank receipts where available.',
        facts: ['PD-08', 'PD-09'],
      },
      {
        painId: painForRow(FUNDER_PAINS, 'P3').painId,
        icon: 'briefcase',
        title: 'Tracks That Follow Employer Demand',
        text: 'An AI-ready curriculum, with entry-level tracks set per country from employer demand, designed to keep pace as AI changes entry-level tasks.',
        facts: ['PD-02', 'PD-10'],
      },
    ]}
  />

  <PhotoGallery id="in-the-field" eyebrow="In the Field" title="Photographs from the Field" lead="Training rooms, laptop handovers and agreements, from past programs." photos={galleryPhotos('youthwide')} />

  <!-- C9 -->
  <FaqSection sources={faqSources} title="Questions Funders and Agencies Ask" />

  <Section id="governance" tone="airy" aria-labelledby="governance-h">
    <SectionHeader id="governance-h" eyebrow="Safeguarding" title="Protected by Design" />
    <CopyP block={SAFEGUARDING} />
    <p><a class="link" href={url('/about/governance/')}>How Governance and Accountability Work<Icon name="arrow-right" size={16} /></a></p>
  </Section>

  <!-- C11: the three options; prices are not published, the budget comes in the discovery session -->
  <OfferSection title="Three Ways to Start, Sized to Your Goals" lead="Each phase is planned with the agency or funder on the results of the one before. We share an indicative budget in the discovery session." options={PROGRAM_OPTIONS} />

  <!-- C12 -->
  <RiskSection title="Start with a Pilot, Then Decide on Evidence">
    <Fragment slot="lead">
      <p data-fact="PD-11">A pilot scorecard is agreed in co-design. Missed thresholds trigger a corrective plan, expansion is your decision, and independent evaluation is welcome.</p>
      <ul class="measures" role="list" aria-label="What the scorecard measures">
        {measures.map((m) => <li><Icon name="circle-check" size={18} />{m}</li>)}
      </ul>
    </Fragment>
  </RiskSection>

  <!-- C13 + C14 (WP24c): ONE "Choose Your Entry Point" chooser (the funders' discovery card holds the page's one primary button; the Bangladesh briefing for
       governments is a text link in its own card, so two primary buttons never stand in one view) and ONE shared "What Happens Next".
       The cards keep the ids #cta and #cta-governments. WP39 (cycle-16 review): the two near-identical session agendas (one in each card) are ONE line under both cards; scripts/check-facts.mjs pins it for the band (#entry-point). -->
  <Section id="entry-point" tone="airy" aria-labelledby="entry-point-h">
    <SectionHeader id="entry-point-h" eyebrow="Get Started" title="Choose Your Entry Point" lead="Funders start with a discovery session. Governments start with a briefing that fits the agency’s timeline." />
    <div class="entry">
      {
        discovery.href && (
          <section id="cta" class="entry__card" aria-labelledby="cta-h" data-reveal>
            <h3 id="cta-h" class="t-heading-l entry__title">Funders: Talk to Us About a First Cohort</h3>
            <div class="entry__actions">
              <Button href={discovery.href} iconEnd="arrow-right">{discovery.label}</Button>
              <a class="link" href={url('/impact/')}>Read the Evidence</a>
            </div>
            {discovery.href.startsWith('mailto:') && <EmailFallback href={discovery.href} />}
            <p class="entry__micro">{MICRO_COMMITMENT}</p>
          </section>
        )
      }
      {
        briefing.href && (
          <section id="cta-governments" class="entry__card" aria-labelledby="cta-governments-h" data-reveal>
            <h3 id="cta-governments-h" class="t-heading-l entry__title">Governments: Start with a Briefing</h3>
            <p class="entry__text">Public procurement follows the agency’s own timeline, so we start with a briefing that fits it.</p>
            <p class="entry__actions">
              <a class="link" href={briefing.href}>{briefing.label}<Icon name="arrow-right" size={16} /></a>
            </p>
            {briefing.href.startsWith('mailto:') && <EmailFallback href={briefing.href} />}
          </section>
        )
      }
    </div>
    <div class="entry__agenda"><SessionAgenda lead="shared" /></div>
  </Section>

  <NextSteps
    steps={[
      { title: 'Briefing or Discovery', text: 'Governments start with a briefing; funders start with a discovery session.' },
      { title: 'Co-Design', text: 'Priority groups, tracks, labs, safeguarding and the scorecard are shaped together with you.' },
      { title: 'Agreement', text: 'Scope, schedule and success measures are agreed, on the agency’s own timeline where it applies.' },
      { title: 'First Cohort', text: 'Training starts in existing labs and colleges on the agreed schedule.' },
      { title: 'Monthly Reports', text: 'Reports are designed to show enrollment, completion, certification, placement and first earnings.' },
    ]}
    roleActions={[
      { role: 'Governments', text: C14.variants.governments },
      { role: 'Funders', text: C14_FIRST },
    ]}
  />

  <Section pad="sm" aria-label="Last updated">
    <p class="updated">Last updated <time datetime={isoDate(LAST_UPDATED)}>{formatDate(LAST_UPDATED)}</time></p>
  </Section>
</LandingLayout>

<style>
  .routes {
    flex-basis: 100%;
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-xs) var(--space-lg);
  }
  /* The Bangladesh band's proof: the 2030 aim (with its "Target" label and fact) beside two figures; one column on a phone, three from 900 px */
  .mech-stats {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-md);
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    align-items: start;
  }
  @media (min-width: 900px) {
    .mech-stats {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }
  }
  /* WP50 (owner design rule 2026-10-16): no left-edge accent bar on the 2030 aim (it was a 4 px tertiary border with a left inset); its "Target" tag and note still set it apart. */
  .mech-target {
    padding: var(--space-xs) 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-xs);
    justify-items: start;
  }
  .mech-target > :global(*) {
    margin: 0;
  }
  .mech-target__note {
    font-size: var(--fs-body-xs);
    color: var(--on-surface-variant);
  }
  .mech-stat {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-xs);
    justify-items: start;
    align-content: start;
  }
  /* Choose Your Entry Point (WP24c): two cards, funders and governments; WP39: one agenda line under both (it replaced two near-identical agendas, one in each card) */
  .entry {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-md);
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    align-items: start;
  }
  @media (min-width: 900px) {
    .entry {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }
  }
  .entry__card {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-sm);
    align-content: start;
    padding: var(--space-md);
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--primary-fixed);
    border-radius: var(--radius-default);
    color: var(--on-surface);
    scroll-margin-top: var(--space-xl);
  }
  .entry__card > :global(*) {
    margin: 0;
  }
  .entry__title {
    color: var(--secondary);
  }
  .entry__text,
  .entry__micro {
    color: var(--on-surface-variant);
  }
  .entry__actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-sm) var(--space-lg);
  }
  /* the shared agenda line sits under both cards, across their full width */
  .entry__agenda :global(.agenda) {
    margin-top: var(--space-md);
    max-width: none;
  }
  .measures {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-sm);
  }
  .measures li {
    display: inline-flex;
    gap: var(--space-sm);
    align-items: center;
    padding: var(--space-sm) var(--space-md);
    border-radius: var(--radius-pill);
    background: var(--primary-fixed);
    color: var(--on-primary-fixed);
    font-weight: var(--fw-medium);
    font-size: var(--fs-body-base);
  }
  .updated {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-md);
    font-size: var(--fs-body-xs);
    color: var(--on-surface-variant);
  }
</style>
